Third-party data in src/data
============================

Files here that Byakugan did not write, where they come from, their licence,
and what we changed. The GGUF model files are not in git: fetch-data.sh
downloads them from this repository's GitHub release, and the same notices
apply to them there.


IAB Tech Lab Content Taxonomy 3.1
---------------------------------
File:     content_taxonomy_3.1.tsv (in git)
Source:   https://github.com/InteractiveAdvertisingBureau/Taxonomies
          "Content Taxonomies/Content Taxonomy 3.1.tsv"
Author:   IAB Technology Laboratory, Inc.
Licence:  Creative Commons Attribution 3.0, as stated in the README of that
          repository: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/
Changes:  none; the file is byte for byte the published one.


Model2Vec potion-base-32M and potion-multilingual-128M
------------------------------------------------------
Files:    potion-base-32M.gguf, potion-multilingual-128M.gguf (release assets)
Source:   https://huggingface.co/minishlab/potion-base-32M
          https://huggingface.co/minishlab/potion-multilingual-128M
Author:   MinishLab (Thomas van Dongen, Stephan Tulkens)
Licence:  MIT, licenses/MIT-model2vec.txt
Changes:  converted by src/convert-models.sh (m2vgguf): the embedding table is
          quantised to Q8_0 and stored with the tokenizer in one GGUF file.


SigLIP 2 base, patch 16, NaFlex
-------------------------------
File:     siglip2-base-patch16-naflex.gguf (release asset)
Source:   https://huggingface.co/google/siglip2-base-patch16-naflex
          revision b53b807d3a2d5e2b3911292f2d69e5341cdc064c
Author:   Google
Licence:  Apache License 2.0, licenses/Apache-2.0.txt
Changes:  converted by src/convert-models.sh (siggguf): the vision tower only,
          its weight matrices quantised to Q8_0, in one GGUF file. The text
          tower is not shipped; siglip2_prototypes.gguf holds the text
          embeddings Byakugan computed with it for every taxonomy node.
